@startuml frontera_y_fallos
' Qué responde este diagrama: "how did you decouple systems, and design
' robust, failure-tolerant agentic systems?"
' Cada punto de fallo marcado abajo tiene un break test que lo ejerce.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #37474F
  LifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
  ParticipantBorderColor #546E7A
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  ParticipantFontColor #263238
}

title Where it can fail, and what happens when it does

actor "Customer" as cli
participant "Qnowa queue\n(Cloud Run)" as portal
participant "Agent graph\n(ADK 2.8)" as grafo
participant "Ceiling\n(pure function)" as techo
participant "Semantic fence\ngemini-embedding-001" as cerco
participant "Co-signer\ngemma-4-26b" as gemma
participant "Cloud KMS" as kms
database "Firestore" as fs
actor "Person\n(own machine)" as humano

cli -> portal : complaint, typed **or spoken**
portal -> grafo : /api/inbound
note right of portal
  A voice note is transcribed and
  then treated as **data**, exactly
  like typed text. The modality
  never widens authority.
end note

grafo -> techo : what is the most this may become?
techo --> grafo : ceiling (deterministic, no model)

grafo -> cerco : does this *mean* human judgement?
alt fence unavailable or slow
  cerco --> grafo : <b>no answer → treat as "needs a human"</b>
  note right : failure closes the door,\nit never opens it
else answers
  cerco --> grafo : may only RAISE caution
end

grafo -> grafo : adjudicate (Gemini) → min(verdict, ceiling)

alt machine may close it
  grafo -> gemma : ALLOW?
  alt DENY, silence, late, or not exactly "ALLOW"
    gemma --> grafo : <b>counts as DENY</b>
    grafo -> fs : pause, wait for a person
    note right of gemma
      The agent cannot sign because it
      cannot control the co-signer.
      Break test: **co-signer**
    end note
  else ALLOW
    grafo -> kms : sign with **clave-agente**
    kms --> grafo : signature
  end
else needs human judgement
  grafo -> kms : try to sign with **clave-humano**
  kms --> grafo : <b>HTTP 403 PERMISSION_DENIED</b>
  note right of kms
    Google refuses, not our code.
    The agent's service account holds
    no binding on the human key.
    Break test: **key-scope**
  end note
  grafo -> fs : pause
  fs --> humano : the case waits
  humano -> humano : signs **on their own machine**
  humano -> grafo : POST /decidir with the signature already made
  note left of humano
    The service verifies it.
    It cannot produce it.
  end note
end

grafo -> grafo : verify (pure function, no network)
grafo -> fs : append to the ledger

note over fs
  <b>If the process dies mid-write</b>, state survives in Firestore
  and the run resumes. Break test: **durability**, 5 steps in 5 processes.
  <b>Altering or reordering a row</b> is detectable: the ledger is chained.
  Break tests: **ledger-chain**, **ledger-order**.
end note

@enduml
